    "fixture": "Amstrad CPC 6128 power-on screen (Amstrad 128K Microcomputer (v3) / 1985 copyright lines / BASIC 1.1 / Ready and the block cursor, yellow on blue) drawn by MAME 0.289's cpc6128 running HOST-NATIVE (drawshm) on the published 1024x768 surface. Reset is a cold boot (MAME_NATIVE_CHECKPOINT=0: the driver has no MACHINE_SUPPORTS_SAVE), which reaches Ready in about 1.1 emulated seconds and is pixel-identical every time; nothing is curated and no keys are sent. Keyboard proved 2026-10-04 through a sandbox daemon with the type-in editor's own edges: a 15-line stress listing (251 shifted symbols, 110 capitals) and all three examples LISTed byte-exact, read back cell by cell against the ROM font, and RUN gave the right result. Keyboard-only exhibit (no mouse); AY-3-8912 -> FIFO."
